  "_commit": {
    "id": "dd471d36b886b56e4d3486f57a868566c1cf2203",
    "author": "tgirke <tgirke@citrus.ucr.edu>",
    "committer": "tgirke <tgirke@citrus.ucr.edu>",
    "message": "Batch + throttle the ChEMBL REST accessors for large ID sets\n\ngetChemblMolecule() and getChemblDrugTarget() previously issued one HTTP\nrequest per input ID. ChEMBL's REST list endpoints (target, mechanism,\ndrug_indication, molecule) all support \"<field>__in=id1,id2,...\" filters,\nso both functions now chunk their IDs (default chunkSize=200, chosen from\nthe server's ~4KB request-line limit measured against httr2's percent-\nencoded comma separators) and paginate each chunk via page_meta, cutting\nrequest counts from O(n) to O(n/chunkSize) for large ID sets.\n\n.dtiApiGET() also gains a client-side req_throttle() cap (5 req/s per\nhost) as a courtesy, since none of these APIs publish a hard rate limit;\nthe existing retry-with-backoff on 429/5xx remains the correctness net.\n\nBatched results are verified to exactly match the prior one-ID-at-a-time\nbehavior (same row set for a shared ID across a batched vs. single call).\n",
    "time": 1784131269
  },
